  "description": "DINKOC crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H62 Co2 Dy4 N8 O32. From the CIF bond table, Co1 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.150-3.928 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.81-111.93°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C48H62Co2Dy4N8O32. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Co(III), Dy(III).",
